    "body": "A native Megatron checkpoint root whose `latest_checkpointed_iteration.txt` contains `0` fails during pretrained initialization with `AssertionError: error parsing metadata file`. Bridge's fallback reader requires a positive iteration even though Core accepts iteration zero and Bridge's resolver treats nonnegative iterations as valid.\n\nAllow zero in the legacy metadata reader. Add resolver-level tests with real tracker files for zero, positive, release, negative and malformed values. Release behavior and invalid-input rejection stay intact. This affects legacy roots without `latest_train_state.pt`; passing a direct iteration directory already bypasses the reader.\n\nSupported path: `checkpoint.pretrained_checkpoint` → `load_checkpoint` / PEFT setup → `_load_checkpoint_from_path` → `_load_base_checkpoint` → `_resolve_checkpoint_iteration` → `read_metadata`. See [checkpoint initialization documentation](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/7e825224f9a955aa11230e42aef115422cea05e7/docs/training/checkpointing.md#L114-L120).\n\nUpstream context: [Core #2199](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/2199) and [#2351](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/2351). Related merged Bridge [#2624](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/pull/2624) adds direct-directory loading; [#5803](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/pull/5803) handles release retention. Neither fixes this legacy-root assertion. Refreshed all-state searches found no exact open Bridge fix.\n\nValidation against Bridge `7e825224f9a955aa11230e42aef115422cea05e7` and its pinned Core `ede2c586cf70dd452f93b9726b31cbedc8df0dd0` (upstream comparison `3630e44a8046c175f3b6f399204755892b84369a`):\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py -k legacy_tracker_contents -q -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\n- Before production change: exit 1; **1 failed, 4 passed**, with only the zero case failing at `AssertionError: error parsing metadata file`. Production matched the recorded base.\n- After change, identical command: exit 0; **5 passed**.\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py -k 'TestCheckpointIterationResolution or TestCheckpointUtilities or TestLoadBaseCheckpoint or TestLoadCheckpointFromPathDirectIterDir' -q -p no:cacheprovider\nuv run pre-commit run --all-files\n```\n\n- Adjacent checkpoint selection, utilities, base loading and direct-directory tests: **53 passed**, exit 0.\n- All-files hooks: **passed**, exit 0, no file modifications.\n- Fresh read-only review: no blocking findings. Native CPU tests exercise file parsing and resolution; full distributed checkpoint payload loading was not run. The change adds no distributed operations.\n\nCore main advanced after discovery to `38a47abb3b7245ff17f98e01379eb5bc40820c50` through test-only #8354; Bridge base and pinned Core remain unchanged. The exact tested sources above are retained.\n",
